- **Explicit non-goals**: {{REJECTED_PATTERNS}} — do not introduce them without
  a written decision record reversing this line.

## Test tiers

Tests are the target function (shared invariant §3). Each tier below is a
distinct signal; naming which one you ran is part of reporting a change.

| Tier | Command | What it proves |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Unit / pure logic | `{{UNIT_TEST_COMMAND}}` | {{UNIT_TEST_SCOPE}} |
| Integration | `{{INTEGRATION_TEST_COMMAND}}` | {{INTEGRATION_TEST_SCOPE}} |
| End-to-end | `{{E2E_TEST_COMMAND}}` | {{E2E_TEST_SCOPE}} |
| Docs gate | `scripts/check.sh` | the manual layer still describes reality |
| Gate self-tests | `scripts/docs-conformance/test/` | the gate itself can still fail |

<!-- The last two rows are real today and are deliberately NOT placeholders:
     they ship with the kit and they work in an empty repo. -->

**Measuring a tier is not a tier** (shared invariant §9). {{MUTATION_TOOL}} asks
whether the first row's tests are load-bearing; run it on demand, never as a
gate — surviving mutants are the objective form of "this test enforces nothing".

